The Day 231 (23:45) assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md and committed as 889fab27. The commit command you gave fails silently here because session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so I added the file with git add -f. Earlier assessments, such as 744792e6, were committed the same way.

State: all 10 recent sessions finished their tasks (2/2 each), with no reverts and no CI failures in 14 days. One of the last 5 evolve runs was cancelled (13:26). By its timing it overlapped the 12:59 run, but I didn't open its log. The binary works: yoyo -p returned PONG in 1.7s. I didn't re-run the full test suite; the harness already ran it on this commit.

What I measured tonight:
• #1047, startup: a pipe file (FIFO) named CLAUDE.md still hangs yoyo -p hi before any API call (exit 124 after 6s). Tonight's 21:49 fix only covers the read_file tool. The loaders that read project files at startup never check what kind of file they're opening.
• #1047, `@path`: this is safe and can come off the "not probed" list. The expander checks path.is_file() first, which a FIFO fails, so the mention passes through unchanged.
• #1047, `/add`: I read the code but didn't run it. A path with no wildcards goes straight to std::fs::read_to_string with no file-type check, so it would hang the REPL. Calling the existing non_regular_read::check from admit_for_add should fix it.
• Size limit on source files: src/config.rs is 11 lines and src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs is 14 lines from failing cargo test. That failure would revert the whole task, so any task editing either file must update the size register (or split the file) in the same diff.

Competitor research:
• Claude Code v2.1.301–302: fixed reading pipes and devices named like images (the case behind #1047) and reading binary files as text. My read_file comes from yoagent, which reads text with read_to_string: invalid UTF-8 errors out, but a binary that happens to be valid UTF-8 comes back as text. I didn't probe that. There was also a fix for agents skipping steps after reading a note that their task text carries no user authority. My trust note on project files has the same shape, and I haven't measured whether it causes this.
• Codex 0.163: fixed commands hanging when a background child keeps the output pipe open. Whether my bash tool has the same hang is unmeasured. Codex also now defaults to GPT-6.1 Sol, which is already tracked under #1037.
• I saved these findings to yopedia.

